One-Line Definitions
Channel

A channel is a layer of image information (Red, Green, Blue).

Filter

A filter is a pattern detector that searches for features such as edges, curves, textures, eyes, or objects.

Depth

Depth is the total number of feature maps/channels present at a layer, usually equal to the number of filters used.

Quick Example
Input Image
224×224×3

Apply 32 Filters

Output
224×224×32
